    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-leverage slate today, with our lineup anchored by high-floor speed threats and favorable matchups against softer rotations. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.37) is our strongest play, boasting a massive boost from a lead-off spot against Cavalli and a dynamic platoon advantage that drives his efficiency well into the \"Strong\" territory. Close behind, **Caleb Durbin** (66.18) remains a high-priority start; his ability to exploit Scherzer\u2019s slow delivery ensures he remains a primary weapon for our stolen base targets. **Christian Yelich** (65.44) also gains significant utility today, as his platoon-adjusted ceiling against Sasaki keeps him well above our 60-point recommended start threshold, even with his projected #6 spot in the order.\n\nThe decision to start **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) over secondary options was driven by his aggressive leadoff placement and a favorable encounter with Abbott\u2019s 5.02 xERA, which provides the highest ceiling for runs scored among our middle infielders. While **Dillon Dingler** (55.35) remains in the marginal bucket, he secured his spot due to the rarity of high-efficiency catching options; his dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Messick narrowly pushed him over the roster threshold. We are monitoring **Trea Turner** (64.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.67) closely, as both carry a 44% rain risk against Bradley; while their offensive projections are high, any significant delay could compromise their game-cap efficiency. \n\nAmong the non-starters, **Colt Keith** was the closest to cracking the lineup but was ultimately benched due to a restrictive L/L platoon disadvantage against Messick, rendering him less efficient than our current middle infield configuration. We are managing our depth carefully to ensure we don't bleed innings, keeping bench assets like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Carson Benge** in reserve as we await the return of starters currently sidelined or facing off-days. We will rely on our depth chart\u2014including **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014should in-game adjustments become necessary based on the weather developments. **Gary Sanchez** (48.01) remains a placeholder pending final lineup confirmation; if his order drops lower than #6, we will be forced to reconsider his viability to maximize our daily cap efficiency.",
